1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:10,040
Sixty-six million years ago, a mountain of rock six miles wide tore through the sky at forty-five thousand miles per hour. Dinosaurs had ten seconds left.

2
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:18,620
It struck Yucatán with the force of one hundred million atomic bombs, instantly vaporizing miles of Earth's crust into a glowing crater.

3
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:29,340
Within five minutes, an infrared heat pulse swept the globe, turning the entire atmosphere into a 1,500-degree broiler oven.

4
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:39,170
Trillions of tons of molten glass tektites rained from orbit, while thousand-foot megatsunamis pulverized continental coastlines.

5
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:49,420
Within twenty-four hours, a choking blanket of soot blocked the sun, plunging the planet into a freezing, decade-long impact winter.

6
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:59,730
Non-avian dinosaurs died out forever. But deep underground, tiny burrowing proto-mammals survived to inherit the earth.

7
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:09,240
In a single afternoon, the asteroid ended an empire. Without it, the human species would never have existed.
